      "text": [
        "3121 - وَ قِيلَ لِلصَّادِقِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : رَجُلٌ فِي ثَوْبِهِ دَمٌ مِمَّا لاَ يَجُوزُ اَلصَّلاَةُ فِي مِثْلِهِ فَطَافَ فِي ثَوْبِهِ فَقَالَ «أَجْزَأَهُ اَلطَّوَافُ فِيهِ ثُمَّ يَنْزِعُهُ وَ يُصَلِّي فِي ثَوْبٍ طَاهِرٍ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3121 - It was said to Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as): \"A man had blood on his garment, of a type that invalidates prayer, and he performed Tawaf in that garment.\"\nImam (as) said: \"His Tawaf is valid, but he should then remove the garment and pray in a pure garment.\""
        ]
      }
